        <title>Adding a Cron Job for Automatic TRIM in Proxmox VE</title>
        <link>https://gowinder.work/en/adding-a-cron-job-for-automatic-trim-in-proxmox-ve/</link>
        <pubDate>Fri, 17 Feb 2023 15:12:05 +0800</pubDate>
        
        <guid>https://gowinder.work/en/adding-a-cron-job-for-automatic-trim-in-proxmox-ve/</guid>
        <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;adding-a-cron-job-for-automatic-trim-in-proxmox-ve&#34;&gt;Adding a Cron Job for Automatic TRIM in Proxmox VE
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;check-the-status&#34;&gt;Check the status
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-shell&#34; data-lang=&#34;shell&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;sudo systemctl status fstrim.timer
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# output:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;● fstrim.timer - Discard unused blocks once a week
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;     Loaded: loaded &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;/lib/systemd/system/fstrim.timer&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; disabled&lt;span class=&#34;p&#34;&gt;;&lt;/span&gt; vendor preset: enabled&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;     Active: inactive &lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;dead&lt;span class=&#34;o&#34;&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;    Trigger: n/a
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;   Triggers: ● fstrim.service
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;       Docs: man:fstrim
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;start-the-service&#34;&gt;Start the service
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-shell&#34; data-lang=&#34;shell&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;sudo systemctl start fstrim.timer
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;check-the-next-cleanup-time&#34;&gt;Check the next cleanup time
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 5
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 6
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 7
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 8
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt; 9
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;10
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;11
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;12
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;13
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;14
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-shell&#34; data-lang=&#34;shell&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;sudo systemctl list-timers --all
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;c1&#34;&gt;# output:&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;NEXT                        LEFT           LAST                        PASSED     UNIT                         ACTIVATES
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;Fri 2023-02-17 23:54:54 CST 8h left        Thu 2023-02-16 23:54:54 CST 15h ago    systemd-tmpfiles-clean.timer systemd-tmpfiles-clean.servi&amp;gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;Sat 2023-02-18 00:00:00 CST 8h left        Fri 2023-02-17 00:00:00 CST 15h ago    atop-rotate.timer            atop-rotate.service
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;Sat 2023-02-18 00:00:00 CST 8h left        Fri 2023-02-17 00:00:00 CST 15h ago    logrotate.timer              logrotate.service
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;Sat 2023-02-18 00:00:00 CST 8h left        Fri 2023-02-17 00:00:00 CST 15h ago    man-db.timer                 man-db.service
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;Sat 2023-02-18 04:19:48 CST 13h left       Fri 2023-02-17 05:29:22 CST 9h ago     pve-daily-update.timer       pve-daily-update.service
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;Sat 2023-02-18 05:18:55 CST 14h left       Fri 2023-02-17 06:45:48 CST 8h ago     apt-daily.timer              apt-daily.service
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;Sat 2023-02-18 06:41:05 CST 15h left       Fri 2023-02-17 06:02:36 CST 9h ago     apt-daily-upgrade.timer      apt-daily-upgrade.service
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;Sun 2023-02-19 03:10:12 CST &lt;span class=&#34;m&#34;&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; day 12h left Sun 2023-02-12 03:10:19 CST &lt;span class=&#34;m&#34;&gt;5&lt;/span&gt; days ago e2scrub_all.timer            e2scrub_all.service
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;Mon 2023-02-20 00:37:59 CST &lt;span class=&#34;m&#34;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt; days left    n/a                         n/a        fstrim.timer                 fstrim.service
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;n/a                         n/a            n/a                         n/a        pvesr.timer
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Done&lt;/p&gt;</description>
        </item>
        <item>
        <title>Rebuilding a GlusterFS Volume</title>
        <link>https://gowinder.work/en/rebuilding-a-glusterfs-volume/</link>
        <pubDate>Thu, 16 Feb 2023 10:53:05 +0800</pubDate>
        
        <guid>https://gowinder.work/en/rebuilding-a-glusterfs-volume/</guid>
        <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;rebuilding-a-glusterfs-volume&#34;&gt;Rebuilding a GlusterFS Volume
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;background&#34;&gt;Background
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;When I first set up the &lt;code&gt;glusterfs&lt;/code&gt; cluster I was in a hurry and used the network addresses of the &lt;code&gt;pve&lt;/code&gt; hosts directly. After a few days I noticed that when &lt;code&gt;volume&lt;/code&gt; replication ran it was saturating the &lt;code&gt;pve&lt;/code&gt; hosts&amp;rsquo; own network channel. The &lt;code&gt;dell r720&lt;/code&gt; happened to have four NICs and the &lt;code&gt;e3&lt;/code&gt; host had two, so I took one from each and dedicated it as the &lt;code&gt;gluster&lt;/code&gt; bind address.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
        </item>
        <item>
        <title>Resolving Gluster Brick Offline Issues</title>
        <link>https://gowinder.work/en/resolving-gluster-brick-offline-issues/</link>
        <pubDate>Sat, 11 Feb 2023 21:13:05 +0800</pubDate>
        
        <guid>https://gowinder.work/en/resolving-gluster-brick-offline-issues/</guid>
        <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;resolving-gluster-brick-offline-issues&#34;&gt;Resolving Gluster Brick Offline Issues
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;offline-issue&#34;&gt;Offline Issue
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;I had just finished installing &lt;code&gt;gluster&lt;/code&gt; and stored the &lt;code&gt;rootfs&lt;/code&gt; of a &lt;code&gt;linux container&lt;/code&gt; on it, so that the &lt;code&gt;linux container&lt;/code&gt; could achieve high availability within a two-node &lt;code&gt;pve&lt;/code&gt; cluster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When I had some spare time, I checked with the command: &lt;code&gt;sudo gluster vol status VMS&lt;/code&gt;, and found that one &lt;code&gt;brick&lt;/code&gt; was in &lt;code&gt;offline&lt;/code&gt; state.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I looked it up online and installed &lt;code&gt;gstatus&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
        </item>
        <item>
        <title>Notes on Deploying a Two-Node HA Cluster and GlusterFS Distributed File System on Proxmox VE</title>
        <link>https://gowinder.work/en/deploying-a-two-node-ha-cluster-and-glusterfs-distributed-file-system-on-proxmox-ve/</link>
        <pubDate>Thu, 09 Feb 2023 14:14:05 +0800</pubDate>
        
        <guid>https://gowinder.work/en/deploying-a-two-node-ha-cluster-and-glusterfs-distributed-file-system-on-proxmox-ve/</guid>
        <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;deploying-a-two-node-ha-cluster-and-glusterfs-distributed-file-system-on-proxmox-ve&#34;&gt;Deploying a Two-Node HA Cluster and GlusterFS Distributed File System on Proxmox VE
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make sure both pve nodes run the same version&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two &lt;code&gt;proxmox ve&lt;/code&gt; nodes, enabling high availability with automatic &lt;code&gt;vm&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;lxc&lt;/code&gt; migration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;edit-the-hosts-file&#34;&gt;Edit the &lt;code&gt;hosts&lt;/code&gt; file
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;In &lt;code&gt;/etc/hosts&lt;/code&gt; on both &lt;code&gt;pve&lt;/code&gt; machines, add the following &lt;code&gt;host&lt;/code&gt; entries:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
&lt;table class=&#34;lntable&#34;&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;3
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;lnt&#34;&gt;4
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&#34;lntd&#34;&gt;
&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-text&#34; data-lang=&#34;text&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;192.168.1.229 pve1.local pve1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;192.168.1.230 pve2.local pve2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;192.168.1.229 gluster1
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;line&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;cl&#34;&gt;192.168.1.230 gluster2
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;install-glusterfs&#34;&gt;Install &lt;code&gt;glusterfs&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The following operations are performed on both machines, referred to here as &lt;code&gt;pve1&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;pve2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
        </item>
        
